# Automatic Railway Gate Controller using Verilog

## Description

This project implements an Automatic Railway Gate Controller using Verilog HDL.

The system uses a train sensor to automatically control the railway gate and
traffic signal lights.

## Features

- Automatic railway gate control
- Train detection using sensor
- Red light when train is detected
- Green light when no train is detected
- Reset functionality
- Verilog testbench for simulation

## Inputs

| Input | Description |
|-------|-------------|
| clk | System clock |
| reset | Reset signal |
| train_sensor | Detects the presence of a train |

## Outputs

| Output | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| gate_open | 1 = Gate Open, 0 = Gate Closed |
| red_light | 1 = Train detected |
| green_light | 1 = No train detected |

## Working

When no train is detected:

- Gate remains OPEN
- Green light is ON
- Red light is OFF

When a train is detected:

- Gate becomes CLOSED
- Red light is ON
- Green light is OFF

After the train passes:

- Gate becomes OPEN
- Green light turns ON
- Red light turns OFF

## Simulation

The design can be simulated using:

- Icarus Verilog
- ModelSim
- QuestaSim
- Vivado

